{%- comment -%}
  Featured products — the "Most Loved" row. A display heading, a micro label
  and a link out, above a grid that reflows on available width.

  The repeated Product card targets only its private Media, data, action, and
  Group blocks. Generic Media is intentionally unavailable inside that card.

  The row is either that grid — unchanged, and the default — or a carousel of
  the same cards. The carousel is **not in the design**: the design's own
  homepage lays Most Loved out as a grid and has no slider anywhere. What is
  the design's is every part of how this one moves, so it reads as the same
  maison rather than as a plugin dropped in:

    - "Slide" is the quick view gallery's motion — one track translated by
      whole pages, `transform 0.6s var(--ease)`.
    - "Fade" is the hero carousel's — the window of cards is swapped in place
      and each one replays `gj-card` (rise and fade, 0.5s) 80ms apart.
    - The arrows are bare and large: a 28px glyph in full ink turning gold,
      centred in the 46px target the design's own row control ("Find by shape")
      is built on — its ring is dropped and its glyph grown in exchange. They
      are gone entirely when there is nothing to cycle through, which is the
      hero's `.hero-carousel.is-static` rule.
      `carousel_arrows` places them under the track, over it, or either side
      of it — and beside the track becomes under it on a narrow row, as the
      hero's own arrows do.

  The marks are a strip that travels rather than a block that wraps, so a
  sixteen-page row still states where you are in one line: the current mark is
  held in the middle of its window and the ones either side half-show past the
  edge. See `.row-carousel__dots` in base.css.

  Nothing here is load-bearing without scripting. The track is the very same
  `.grid-auto grid-auto--products` element in both layouts, so a visitor with
  no JavaScript gets the grid — every card in it, every link real — and the
  controls, which would be a lie, never appear.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign collection = collections[section.settings.collection]

  comment
    How many pieces the row shows. Off by default the section shows the whole
    collection; `limit_products` is what brings the count setting into play,
    and the editor only offers that setting while it is on.

    Shopify caps an un-paginated `collection.products` loop at 50 whatever is
    asked for, so "all" means "up to 50" — the same ceiling the collection
    template lives with.

    The placeholder branch below still needs a number when there is no
    collection to count, so the setting's own value stands in there.
  endcomment
  assign limit = section.settings.products_to_show
  unless section.settings.limit_products
    if collection != blank
      assign limit = collection.all_products_count
    endif
  endunless

  assign is_carousel = false
  if section.settings.layout == 'carousel'
    assign is_carousel = true
  endif

  comment
    How many cards are actually rendered — and so, at one card per page, the
    most pages the carousel can ever have. The dots are rendered by Liquid
    like everything else and the script only hides the surplus.
  endcomment
  assign card_count = limit
  if collection.products.size > 0
    assign card_count = collection.products.size
    if card_count > limit
      assign card_count = limit
    endif
  endif

  comment
    The carousel's accessible name. There is no heading setting to borrow from
    any more — the heading is a block, and a section cannot read one — so it
    falls back to the theme's own label rather than guessing at a block's text.
    Same answer collection-list reached when it converted.
  endcomment
  assign carousel_label = 'general.carousel.label' | t
-%}

<section
  class="section scheme-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}{% if section.settings.full_height %} section--tall{% endif %}"
  style="{% render 'section-style', padding_top: section.settings.padding_top, padding_bottom: section.settings.padding_bottom %} {%- if section.settings.content_alignment != blank and section.settings.content_alignment != 'inherit' -%}--section-align: {{ section.settings.content_alignment }}; --section-align-jc: {% if section.settings.content_alignment == 'center' %}center{% elsif section.settings.content_alignment == 'right' %}flex-end{% else %}flex-start{% endif %};{%- endif -%}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    **The header is blocks, and the row they used to share is now the
    container's job.** This section resisted conversion for one reason: its
    subheading and its "View All" link share a single `space-between` row, and
    merchant blocks can only render as one flat sibling flow — made into blocks
    they would fall onto two lines.

    **The `group` block answers it, and generally rather than here.** A layout
    group is a block that arranges other blocks, so the eyebrow and the button
    go *inside* one and the group puts them on a row and pushes them apart. The
    merchant can see it, move it, and use the same thing anywhere else — which
    is why this is not a rule in the stylesheet named after this section.

    "View All" is a `button` block now rather than a bespoke link, with its
    destination stored in its ordinary Link setting. There is no second source
    picker or section-aware fallback hidden behind the block.

    The section owns the vertical rhythm: one `gap` spaces every direct child,
    each header block and the row itself. That also retires `.display +
    .grid-auto` here — an adjacency rule a wrapper would break — exactly as
    `collection-list` already does.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="page-width products-list__content" style="{% render 'block-spacing', gap: section.settings.gap %}">
    {% content_for 'blocks' %}

    {%- comment -%}
      The column floor is `.grid-auto--products`' own now, so both layouts and
      every other product grid read one rule. The carousel works out how many
      cards fit by measuring a hidden box carrying that same expression, so the
      two can never disagree about a column count.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture grid_vars -%}
      --gap: var(--grid-gap);
    {%- endcapture -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      **The card is one block, not one per product**, exactly as the collection
      list's is. `_product-card` is a *static* block rendered once per piece
      inside this loop, handed the piece it is for through `closest.product`.
      Eight pieces show eight cards from one set of settings, and the theme
      editor lists the card once with the repeat mark.

      That is also what lets this section keep the carousel. Merchant-added
      blocks render as one flat sibling flow, so a header block and a moving
      track could never share a section — but the section is doing the looping
      here, so it can still wrap each card in the cell the carousel needs.

      The cards are identical in both layouts. In the grid each one carries its
      own `.reveal` and the design's 60ms stagger; in the carousel the component
      reveals as a whole and the cards' entrance is `gj-card`, staggered by
      their place in the visible page.

      **The loop is written twice, deliberately**, as the collection list's is:
      the carousel takes its cells as markup and so has to capture them, and the
      grid — the default — must not depend on `{% content_for %}` surviving a
      capture. Keep the two the same.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      **One render site per layout, and that is a rule rather than a tidy-up.**
      `theme check`'s `UniqueStaticBlockId` fails a section that names the same
      static block id twice in the same branch, so the real cards and the
      onboarding placeholders cannot be two loops as they were when this
      section rendered a snippet.

      They do not need to be. `card_count` is already `min(products, limit)`
      where there are products and `limit` where there are none, so one loop
      over it produces exactly what the two did: a card per piece, or a row of
      placeholders. Indexing past the end hands the block a nil product, which
      is the placeholder every card block already renders.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if is_carousel -%}
      {%- capture cards -%}
        {%- for i in (1..card_count) -%}
          {%- assign card_product = collection.products[forloop.index0] -%}
          <div class="row-carousel__cell" data-row-cell>
            {% content_for 'block', type: '_product-card', id: 'product-card', closest.product: card_product %}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- render 'row-carousel',
        cells: cards,
        count: card_count,
        motion: section.settings.carousel_motion,
        arrows: section.settings.carousel_arrows,
        label: carousel_label,
        track_class: 'grid-auto--products',
        track_style: grid_vars
      -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="grid-auto grid-auto--products" style="{{ grid_vars | strip }}">
        {%- for i in (1..card_count) -%}
          {%- assign card_product = collection.products[forloop.index0] -%}
          <div class="reveal" style="--reveal-delay: {{ forloop.index0 | times: 60 }}ms;">
            {% content_for 'block', type: '_product-card', id: 'product-card', closest.product: card_product %}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.featured_products.name",
  "tag": "div",
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@app" },
    { "type": "text" },
    { "type": "rich-text" },
    { "type": "group" },
    { "type": "button" }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "content_alignment",
      "label": "t:sections.all.content_alignment.label",
      "info": "t:sections.all.content_alignment.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "left", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.left" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.center" },
        { "value": "right", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.right" }
      ],
      "default": "left"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:sections.all.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme_1"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.collection.label"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "layout",
      "label": "t:sections.all.layout.label",
      "info": "t:sections.all.layout.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "grid",
          "label": "t:sections.all.layout.grid"
        },
        {
          "value": "carousel",
          "label": "t:sections.all.layout.carousel"
        }
      ],
      "default": "grid"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "carousel_motion",
      "label": "t:sections.all.carousel_motion.label",
      "info": "t:sections.all.carousel_motion.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "slide",
          "label": "t:sections.all.carousel_motion.slide"
        },
        {
          "value": "fade",
          "label": "t:sections.all.carousel_motion.fade"
        }
      ],
      "default": "slide",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "carousel_arrows",
      "label": "t:sections.all.carousel_arrows.label",
      "info": "t:sections.all.carousel_arrows.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "bottom",
          "label": "t:sections.all.carousel_arrows.bottom"
        },
        {
          "value": "top",
          "label": "t:sections.all.carousel_arrows.top"
        },
        {
          "value": "side",
          "label": "t:sections.all.carousel_arrows.side"
        }
      ],
      "default": "bottom",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.layout == 'carousel' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "limit_products",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.limit_products.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_products.limit_products.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "products_to_show",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_products.products_to_show.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.limit_products }}",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 50,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 8
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:blocks.all.gap.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.all.gap.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.none" },
        { "value": "minimal", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.minimal" },
        { "value": "tiny", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.tiny" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.small" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.medium" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.large" },
        { "value": "xlarge", "label": "t:blocks.all.step.xlarge" }
      ],
      "default": "large"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "full_height",
      "label": "t:sections.all.full_height.label",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.all.spacing_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding_top.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.none" },
        { "value": "2xs", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.2xs" },
        { "value": "xs", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.xs" },
        { "value": "sm", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.sm" },
        { "value": "md", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.md" },
        { "value": "lg", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.lg" },
        { "value": "xl", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.xl" },
        { "value": "max", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.max" }
      ],
      "default": "sm"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:sections.all.padding_bottom.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.none" },
        { "value": "2xs", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.2xs" },
        { "value": "xs", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.xs" },
        { "value": "sm", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.sm" },
        { "value": "md", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.md" },
        { "value": "lg", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.lg" },
        { "value": "xl", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.xl" },
        { "value": "max", "label": "t:sections.all.space_step.max" }
      ],
      "default": "sm"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:sections.featured_products.name",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "text", "settings": { "text": "Most Loved", "style": "title", "layout": "display", "element": "h2" } },
        {
          "type": "group",
          "blocks": [
            { "type": "text", "settings": { "text": "Our most loved creations", "style": "subheading", "layout": "eyebrow", "element": "span" } },
            {
              "type": "button",
              "settings": {
                "button_label": "View All",
                "button_link": "/collections/all",
                "button_style": "arrow"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "_product-card",
          "static": true,
          "id": "product-card",
          "blocks": [
            { "type": "_product-card-media" },
            { "type": "text", "settings": { "text": "{{ closest.product.title }}", "style": "small", "element": "h3", "override_case": "uppercase", "override_tracking": "wide" } },
            { "type": "_product-card-option-control", "settings": { "target_by": "auto" } },
            { "type": "_product-card-price" },
            { "type": "_product-card-add", "settings": { "variant_action": "choose_options" } }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
